<title>USA: DCR rates Mendoza foreign currency Double-B-Minus.</title>
<headline>DCR rates Mendoza foreign currency Double-B-Minus.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps Credit Rating Co said Monday it assigned a rating of Double-B-Minus to the foreign currency obligations of the Mendoza province, Argentina.</p>
<p>DCR said the rating is supported by Mendoza's diversified economic base, conservative fiscal policy and low level of total debt.</p>
<p>In general, Mendoza has closely followed Argentina's growth, DCR said. It rates the foreign currency obligations of Argentina at Double-B.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
